1-40cc-8c17-1e92cb72a9ef",536870920]],["^15",[1437,"^3","#+TAGS: python, sqlserver\n\n# referencia por si se borra ese comentario:\n\n<https://github.com/mkleehammer/pyodbc/issues/610#issuecomment-1730853990>\n\nI am using amazon Linux for deploying Python with elastic beanstalk.\nI am facing the same problem.\nIn Red Hat (in my case amazon Linux), you must configure /etc/pki/tls/openssl.cnf.\n\nFirst, add or change,\n\n`openssl_conf = default_conf`\n\nAnd add to last line\n\n```\n[default_conf]\nssl_conf = ssl_sect\n\n[ssl_sect]\nsystem_default = system_default_sect\n\n[system_default_sect]\nMinProtocol = TLSv1.2\nCipherString = DEFAULT@SECLEVEL=1\n```\n",536870920]],["^15",[1437,"^17",1746025480316,536870920]],["^15",[1437,"^Z","pages/problema con ssl en pyodbc usando driver sqlserver.md",536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^K",1746025480316,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^[",1437,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^Y","problema con ssl en pyodbc usando driver sqlserver",536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^11","problema con ssl en pyodbc usando driver sqlserver",536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^?",["^ ","^19",["^1:",["python","sqlserver"]]],536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^4",["^ ","^19","python, sqlserver"],536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^P",423,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^P",1439,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^B",1746025480316,536870920]],["^15",[1438,"^;","~u68123c08-454c-4d18-8254-e630ebd2e83c",536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^K",1746025480432,536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^[",1603,536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^Y","sqlserver",536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^11","sqlserver",536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^?",["^ ","^19",["^1:",["database"]]],536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^4",["^ ","^19","#database"],536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^P",463,536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^B",1746025480432,536870920]],["^15",[1439,"^;","~u68123c08-8bba-4fe9-81a6-a65842560d97",536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^Q","#+TAGS: python, sqlserver\n\n",536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^1;",["^1:",[]],536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^F",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^X",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^V",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^U",423,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^U",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^U",1439,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^:",true,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^?",["^ ","^19",["^1:",["python","sqlserver"]]],536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^J",["^19"],536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^4",["^ ","^19","python, sqlserver"],536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^H",423,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^H",1439,536870920]],["^15",[1440,"^;","~u68123c08-0076-456d-9c05-aab1d718441b",536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^Q","# referencia por si se borra ese comentario:\n\n<https://github.com/mkleehammer/pyodbc/issues/610#issuecomment-1730853990>\n\nI am using amazon Linux for deploying Python with elastic beanstalk.\nI am facing the same problem.\nIn Red Hat (in my case amazon Linux), you must configure /etc/pki/tls/openssl.cnf.\n\nFirst, add or change,\n\n`openssl_conf = default_conf`\n\nAnd add to last line\n\n```\n[default_conf]\nssl_conf = ssl_sect\n\n[ssl_sect]\nsystem_default = system_default_sect\n\n[system_default_sect]\nMinProtocol = TLSv1.2\nCipherString = DEFAULT@SECLEVEL=1\n```",536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^F",1440,536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^X",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^V",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^U",1438,536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^?",["^ ","^1<",1],536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1441,"^;","~u68123c08-e498-4640-b204-e6647c480726",536870920]],["^15",[1442,"^3","- [[Lsof]] lists on its standard output file information about files opened by processes.\n\t- este video es interesante {{video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n9nZ1ellaV0}}",536870920]],["^15",[1442,"^17",1746025480323,536870920]],["^15",[1442,"^Z","pages/process monitoring.md",536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^K",1746025480323,536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^Y","lsof",536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^11","Lsof",536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^B",1746025480323,536870920]],["^15",[1443,"^;","~u68123c08-5507-4ec9-b1ed-502579851edf",536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^Q","[[Lsof]] lists on its standard output file information about files opened by processes.",536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^F",911,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^X",911,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^V",911,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^U",911,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^U",1443,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^H",1443,536870920]],["^15",[1444,"^;","~u68123c08-fde1-4f90-99de-7bddd7291e12",536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^Q","este video es interesante {{video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n9nZ1ellaV0}}",536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^F",1444,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^S",1446,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^X",911,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^V",1444,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^U",911,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^U",1443,536870920]],["^15",[1445,"^;","~u68123c08-0274-4600-a440-2d23f47575da",536870920]],["^15",[1446,"^?",["^ ","~:logseq.macro-name","video","~:logseq.macro-arguments",["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n9nZ1ellaV0"]],536870920]],["^15",[1446,"^W","macro",536870920]],["^15",[1446,"^T","video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n9nZ1ellaV0",536870920]],["^15",[1447,"^3","- Prometheus is an open-source systems monitoring and alerting toolkit designed for reliability and scalability.\n- It features a multi-dimensional data model, a flexible query language (PromQL), and an efficient time series database.\n- Prometheus collects metrics from configured targets at given intervals, evaluates rule expressions, displays results, and can trigger alerts when specified conditions are observed.\n- It operates on a pull model, scraping metrics from HTTP endpoints, and supports service discovery for dynamic environments.\n- Prometheus is particularly well-suited for monitoring microservices and containerized environments, integrating seamlessly with systems like Kubernetes.\n- Its ecosystem includes various exporters for third-party systems and a built-in alert manager.\n- Widely adopted in cloud-native architectures, Prometheus is a core component of modern observability stacks, often used alongside tools like Grafana for visualization.",536870920]],["^15",[1447,"^17",1746025480329,536870920]],["^15",[1447,"^Z","pages/prometheus.md",536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^Q","Prometheus is an open-source systems monitoring and alerting toolkit designed for reliability and scalability.",536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^F",913,536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1448,"^;","~u68123c08-77d6-4f98-94c1-747cad9caf31",536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^Q","It features a multi-dimensional data model, a flexible query language (PromQL), and an efficient time series database.",536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^F",1448,536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1449,"^;","~u68123c08-c99d-44a2-ae6c-1e76f629b272",536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^Q","Prometheus collects metrics from configured targets at given intervals, evaluates rule expressions, displays results, and can trigger alerts when specified conditions are observed.",536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^F",1449,536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1450,"^;","~u68123c08-9bc9-4c99-a29a-8a060e432d53",536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^Q","It operates on a pull model, scraping metrics from HTTP endpoints, and supports service discovery for dynamic environments.",536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^F",1450,536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1451,"^;","~u68123c08-735b-4e39-a987-45ad53c0b007",536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^Q","Prometheus is particularly well-suited for monitoring microservices and containerized environments, integrating seamlessly with systems like Kubernetes.",536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^F",1451,536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1452,"^;","~u68123c08-9be1-4a7f-92f7-59dc2b63be78",536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^Q","Its ecosystem includes various exporters for third-party systems and a built-in alert manager.",536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^F",1452,536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1453,"^;","~u68123c08-e91c-468d-aa8b-15d116d65693",536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^Q","Widely adopted in cloud-native architectures, Prometheus is a core component of modern observability stacks, often used alongside tools like Grafana for visualization.",536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^F",1453,536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^X",913,536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^V",913,536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^U",913,536870920]],["^15",[1454,"^;","~u68123c08-10cb-4947-ac8d-bbd9f1e98b60",536870920]],["^15",[1455,"^3","- Provisioning refers to the process of setting up and configuring the necessary IT infrastructure to support an application or service.\n- This includes allocating and preparing resources such as servers, storage, networking, and software environments.\n- Provisioning can be done manually, but in modern DevOps practices, it’s typically automated using tools like Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation.\n- These tools allow for infrastructure-as-code, where the entire provisioning process is defined in version-controlled scripts or templates.\n- This approach enables consistent, repeatable deployments across different environments, reduces human error, and facilitates rapid scaling and disaster recovery.",536870920]],["^15",[1455,"^17",1746025480332,536870920]],["^15",[1455,"^Z","pages/provisioning.md",536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^Q","Provisioning refers to the process of setting up and configuring the necessary IT infrastructure to support an application or service.",536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^F",933,536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^X",933,536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^V",933,536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^U",933,536870920]],["^15",[1456,"^;","~u68123c08-746b-418c-b272-f4a0c948a69f",536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^Q","This includes allocating and preparing resources such as servers, storage, networking, and software environments.",536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^F",1456,536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^X",933,536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^V",933,536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^U",933,536870920]],["^15",[1457,"^;","~u68123c08-4d38-440c-96d6-f6b6573f8e97",536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^Q","Provisioning can be done manually, but in modern DevOps practices, it’s typically automated using tools like Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation.",536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^F",1457,536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^X",933,536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^V",933,536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^U",933,536870920]],["^15",[1458,"^;","~u68123c08-9a0d-41a5-bddd-bb8d2f302409",536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^Q","These tools allow for infrastructure-as-code, where the entire provisioning process is defined in version-controlled scripts or templates.",536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^F",1458,536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^X",933,536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^V",933,536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^U",933,536870920]],["^15",[1459,"^;","~u68123c08-7c88-4efa-a677-89cdb662af72",536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^Q","This approach enables consistent, repeatable deployments across different environments, reduces human error, and facilitates rapid scaling and disaster recovery.",536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^F",1459,536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^X",933,536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^V",933,536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^U",933,536870920]],["^15",[1460,"^;","~u68123c08-82bb-42e5-bb04-f96a220cae68",536870920]],["^15",[1461,"^3","- Pulumi is an open-source infrastructure as code (IaC) platform that allows developers to define and manage cloud resources using familiar programming languages like JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Go, and .NET languages.\n- It supports multiple cloud providers including AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, and Kubernetes.\n- Pulumi’s approach enables developers to use standard programming constructs such as loops, functions, and classes to create reusable and modular infrastructure code.\n- It provides a unified workflow for deploying and managing resources across different cloud environments, offering features like state management, drift detection, and preview of changes before deployment.\n- Pulumi’s ecosystem includes a registry of pre-built components and integrations with CI/CD systems, making it a powerful tool for teams adopting DevOps practices and managing complex, multi-cloud infrastructures.",536870920]],["^15",[1461,"^17",1746025480341,536870920]],["^15",[1461,"^Z","pages/pulumi.md",536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^Q","Pulumi is an open-source infrastructure as code (IaC) platform that allows developers to define and manage cloud resources using familiar programming languages like JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Go, and .NET languages.",536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^F",935,536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^X",935,536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^V",935,536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^U",935,536870920]],["^15",[1462,"^;","~u68123c08-8080-477d-be63-ecfe0bca7812",536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^Q","It supports multiple cloud providers including AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, and Kubernetes.",536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^F",1462,536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^X",935,536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^V",935,536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^U",935,536870920]],["^15",[1463,"^;","~u68123c08-1e0e-4e92-8d0f-06bde9989972",536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^Q","Pulumi’s approach enables developers to use standard programming constructs such as loops, functions, and classes to create reusable and modular infrastructure code.",536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^F",1463,536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^X",935,536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^V",935,536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^U",935,536870920]],["^15",[1464,"^;","~u68123c08-d34a-4f42-aaef-456706599a81",536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^Q","It provides a unified workflow for deploying and managing resources across different cloud environments, offering features like state management, drift detection, and preview of changes before deployment.",536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^F",1464,536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^X",935,536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^V",935,536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^U",935,536870920]],["^15",[1465,"^;","~u68123c08-5ef0-42cd-83cb-a78bf67f9364",536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^Q","Pulumi’s ecosystem includes a registry of pre-built components and integrations with CI/CD systems, making it a powerful tool for teams adopting DevOps practices and managing complex, multi-cloud infrastructures.",536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^F",1465,536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^X",935,536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^V",935,536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^U",935,536870920]],["^15",[1466,"^;","~u68123c08-ed32-49a3-a568-1abbf849e22b",536870920]],["^15",[1467,"^3","- Python es un lenguaje de alto nivel de programación interpretado cuya filosofía hace hincapié en la legibilidad de su código. Se trata de un lenguaje de programación multiparadigma, ya que soporta parcialmente la orientación a objetos, programación imperativa y, en menor medida, programación funcional. Es un lenguaje interpretado, dinámico y multiplataforma.",536870920]],["^15",[1467,"^17",1746025480343,536870920]],["^15",[1467,"^Z","pages/python.md",536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^Q","Python es un lenguaje de alto nivel de programación interpretado cuya filosofía hace hincapié en la legibilidad de su código. Se trata de un lenguaje de programación multiparadigma, ya que soporta parcialmente la orientación a objetos, programación imperativa y, en menor medida, programación funcional. Es un lenguaje interpretado, dinámico y multiplataforma.",536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^F",423,536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^X",423,536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^V",423,536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^U",423,536870920]],["^15",[1468,"^;","~u68123c08-58c3-4ef8-8b76-5c330784307c",536870920]],["^15",[1469,"^3","#+TAGS: javascript, framework, react\n\n- # [Remix](https://remix.run/)\n- ## que es remix\n\n  Remix is a full stack web framework that lets you focus on the user interface and work back through web standards to deliver a fast, slick, and resilient user experience. People are gonna love using your stuff.\n\n- ## instalacion\n\n  Para instalarlo se puede usar el clasico create-\\* como el resto.\n\n  ```bash\n  npx create-remix@latest\n  ```\n\n- ## Root Route\n\n  Esto es lo que llamamos la \"Ruta Raíz\". Es el primer componente de la interfaz de usuario que se representa, por lo que normalmente contiene el diseño global de la página.\n\n- ## Adding Stylesheets with `links`\n\n  Si bien hay varias formas de diseñar tu aplicación Remix, usaremos una hoja de estilo simple que ya ha sido escrita para mantener todo enfocado en Remix.\n  Puede importar archivos CSS directamente a módulos JavaScript. El compilador tomará las huellas digitales del activo, lo guardará en su [`assetsBuildDirectory`](https://remix.run/docs/en/main/file-conventions/remix-config#assetsbuilddirectory) y le proporcionará a su módulo el href de acceso público.\n  Cada ruta puede exportar una función de [`links`](https://remix.run/docs/en/main/route/links). Se recopilarán y representarán en el componente `<Links />` que representamos en app/root.tsx.\n  La aplicación debería verse así ahora. Seguro que es bueno tener un diseñador que también pueda escribir CSS, ¿no? (Gracias, Jim 🙏).\n\n- ## Routes\n\n  En la convención de archivos de ruta Remix, `.` creará un `/` en la URL y `$` hará que un segmento sea dinámico.\n  Acabamos de crear una ruta que coincidirá con URL que se ven así:\n  `/contactos/123`\n  `/contactos/abc`\n  como se puede ver en la siguinete image, al tener una route de la forma `character._index.tsx` la ruta que va a crear va a ser /character y la otra ruta va a ser `/character/characterid` siendo las dos rutas diferentes. para los casos que solo se tenga un `character.tsx` y un `character.$characterid.tsx` el character.tsx seria el template y la otra ruta seria el children que recibe en el outlet.\n\n  ![[Pasted image 20240128180024.png]]\n",536870920]],["^15",[1469,"^17",1746025480354,536870920]],["^15",[1469,"^Z","pages/remix.md",536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^K",1746025480353,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^[",1469,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^Y","remix",536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^11","remix",536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^?",["^ ","^19",["^1:",["javascript","framework","react"]]],536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^4",["^ ","^19","javascript, framework, react"],536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^P",539,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^P",1046,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^P",1471,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^B",1746025480353,536870920]],["^15",[1470,"^;","~u68123c08-32a1-484e-ab2a-63749ddeaa74",536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^K",1746025480353,536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^Y","react",536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^11","react",536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^B",1746025480353,536870920]],["^15",[1471,"^;","~u68123c08-6e5a-4884-b956-ea86b011666b",536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^K",1746025480354,536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^@",false,536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^Y","pasted image 20240128180024.png",536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^11","Pasted image 20240128180024.png",536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^B",1746025480354,536870920]],["^15",[1472,"^;","~u68123c08-910e-4b51-b994-243f809d2828",536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^Q","#+TAGS: javascript, framework, react\n\n",536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^1;",["^1:",[]],536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^F",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^U",539,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^U",1046,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^U",1471,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^:",true,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^?",["^ ","^19",["^1:",["javascript","framework","react"]]],536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^J",["^19"],536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^4",["^ ","^19","javascript, framework, react"],536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^H",539,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^H",1046,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^H",1471,536870920]],["^15",[1473,"^;","~u68123c08-8ca1-46ca-932c-7e9341883ae2",536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^Q","# [Remix](https://remix.run/)",536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^F",1473,536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^?",["^ ","^1<",1],536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1474,"^;","~u68123c08-e5af-4ad1-b9cf-c6e213fe17dc",536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^Q","## que es remix\n\nRemix is a full stack web framework that lets you focus on the user interface and work back through web standards to deliver a fast, slick, and resilient user experience. People are gonna love using your stuff.",536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^F",1474,536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^?",["^ ","^1<",2],536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1475,"^;","~u68123c08-b1ed-4c41-9041-611017856d5c",536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^Q","## instalacion\n\nPara instalarlo se puede usar el clasico create-\\* como el resto.\n\n```bash\nnpx create-remix@latest\n```",536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^F",1475,536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^?",["^ ","^1<",2],536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1476,"^;","~u68123c08-76f7-4e2d-8df7-0912b697efe7",536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^Q","## Root Route\n\nEsto es lo que llamamos la \"Ruta Raíz\". Es el primer componente de la interfaz de usuario que se representa, por lo que normalmente contiene el diseño global de la página.",536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^F",1476,536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^?",["^ ","^1<",2],536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1477,"^;","~u68123c08-db52-49d2-a0e0-efd054d12980",536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^Q","## Adding Stylesheets with `links`\n\nSi bien hay varias formas de diseñar tu aplicación Remix, usaremos una hoja de estilo simple que ya ha sido escrita para mantener todo enfocado en Remix.\nPuede importar archivos CSS directamente a módulos JavaScript. El compilador tomará las huellas digitales del activo, lo guardará en su [`assetsBuildDirectory`](https://remix.run/docs/en/main/file-conventions/remix-config#assetsbuilddirectory) y le proporcionará a su módulo el href de acceso público.\nCada ruta puede exportar una función de [`links`](https://remix.run/docs/en/main/route/links). Se recopilarán y representarán en el componente `<Links />` que representamos en app/root.tsx.\nLa aplicación debería verse así ahora. Seguro que es bueno tener un diseñador que también pueda escribir CSS, ¿no? (Gracias, Jim 🙏).",536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^F",1477,536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^?",["^ ","^1<",2],536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1478,"^;","~u68123c08-9801-4dbf-9483-bbad469ef42d",536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^Q","## Routes\n\nEn la convención de archivos de ruta Remix, `.` creará un `/` en la URL y `$` hará que un segmento sea dinámico.\nAcabamos de crear una ruta que coincidirá con URL que se ven así:\n`/contactos/123`\n`/contactos/abc`\ncomo se puede ver en la siguinete image, al tener una route de la forma `character._index.tsx` la ruta que va a crear va a ser /character y la otra ruta va a ser `/character/characterid` siendo las dos rutas diferentes. para los casos que solo se tenga un `character.tsx` y un `character.$characterid.tsx` el character.tsx seria el template y la otra ruta seria el children que recibe en el outlet.\n\n![[Pasted image 20240128180024.png]]",536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^F",1478,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^X",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^V",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^U",1470,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^U",1472,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^?",["^ ","^1<",2],536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^J",[],536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^H",1472,536870920]],["^15",[1479,"^;","~u68123c08-7790-42be-a87a-f75caed8530b",536870920]],["^15",[1480,"^3","",536870920]],["^15",[1480,"^17",1746025480358,536870920]],["^15",[1480,"^Z","pages/sas.md",536870920]],["^15",[1481,"^3","- Secret management refers to the secure handling, storage, and distribution of sensitive information such as passwords, API keys, and certificates within an organization’s IT infrastructure.\n- It involves using specialized tools and practices to protect secrets from unauthorized access while ensuring they are available to authorized systems and users when needed.\n- Secret management solutions typically offer features like encryption at rest and in transit, access controls, auditing, rotation policies, and integration with various platforms and services.\n- These systems aim to centralize secret storage, reduce the risk of exposure, automate secret lifecycle management, and provide seamless integration with applications and DevOps workflows. Effective secret management is crucial for maintaining security, compliance, and operational efficiency in modern, complex IT environments.",536870920]],["^15",[1481,"^17",1746025480362,536870920]],["^15",[1481,"^Z","pages/secret management.md",536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^Q","Secret management refers to the secure handling, storage, and distribution of sensitive information such as passwords, API keys, and certificates within an organization’s IT infrastructure.",536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^F",945,536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^X",945,536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^V",945,536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^U",945,536870920]],["^15",[1482,"^;","~u68123c08-adae-4ab4-a0c3-23446d27f7bd",536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^Q","It involves using specialized tools and practices to protect secrets from unauthorized access while ensuring they are available to authorized systems and users when needed.",536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^F",1482,536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^X",945,536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^V",945,536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^U",945,536870920]],["^15",[1483,"^;","~u68123c08-f244-49e8-8ab5-7c6ce395cb9b",536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^Q","Secret management solutions typically offer features like encryption at rest and in transit, access controls, auditing, rotation policies, and integration with various platforms and services.",536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^F",1483,536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^X",945,536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^V",945,536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^U",945,536870920]],["^15",[1484,"^;","~u68123c08-9953-43c2-aa41-6cfd078ed0a6",536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^Q","These systems aim to centralize secret storage, reduce the risk of exposure, automate secret lifecycle management, and provide seamless integration with applications and DevOps workflows. Effective secret management is crucial for maintaining security, compliance, and operational efficiency in modern, complex IT environments.",536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^F",1484,536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^X",945,536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^V",945,536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^U",945,536870920]],["^15",[1485,"^;","~u68123c08-18a1-4294-8799-33071cc28d98",536870920]],["^15",[1486,"^3","- Serverless is a cloud-computing execution model where the cloud provider dynamically manages the infrastructure, allowing developers to focus solely on writing code.\n- In this model, resources are automatically allocated and scaled based on demand, and billing is based on actual usage rather than pre-purchased capacity.\n- Serverless architectures are often used for event-driven workloads and microservices, improving development efficiency and reducing operational overhead.\n- Popular platforms for serverless computing include AWS Lambda, Azure Functions, and Google Cloud Functions.",536870920]],["^15",[1486,"^17",1746025480365,536870920]],["^15",[1486,"^Z","pages/serverless.md",536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^Q","Serverless is a cloud-computing execution model where the cloud provider dynamically manages the infrastructure, allowing developers to focus solely on writing code.",536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^F",949,536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^X",949,536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^V",949,536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^U",949,536870920]],["^15",[1487,"^;","~u68123c08-943f-449c-8809-a753cc051ba9",536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^Q","In this model, resources are automatically allocated and scaled based on demand, and billing is based on actual usage rather than pre-purchased capacity.",536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^F",1487,536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^X",949,536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^V",949,536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^U",949,536870920]],["^15",[1488,"^;","~u68123c08-72b9-45bf-a282-7dfe16d10fff",536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^Q","Serverless architectures are often used for event-driven workloads and microservices, improving development efficiency and reducing operational overhead.",536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^F",1488,536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^X",949,536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^V",949,536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^U",949,536870920]],["^15",[1489,"^;","~u68123c08-1af1-4be2-8322-01a06f25e81f",536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^Q","Popular platforms for serverless computing include AWS Lambda, Azure Functions, and Google Cloud Functions.",536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^F",1489,536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^X",949,536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^V",949,536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^U",949,536870920]],["^15",[1490,"^;","~u68123c08-ce1f-4de0-82cc-fb9e3ea41768",536870920]],["^15",[1491,"^3","- A service mesh is a dedicated infrastructure layer that manages communication between microservices in a distributed application.\n- It provides features like load balancing, service discovery, encryption, observability, and traffic management, allowing services to communicate securely and efficiently.\n- By abstracting network-related concerns from the application code, a service mesh enhances reliability and security while simplifying the management of microservice interactions.\n- Popular service mesh implementations include Istio, Linkerd, and Consul.",536870920]],["^15",[1491,"^17",1746025480373,536870920]],["^15",[1491,"^Z","pages/service mesh.md",536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^Q","A service mesh is a dedicated infrastructure layer that manages communication between microservices in a distributed application.",536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^F",901,536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^X",901,536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^V",901,536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^U",901,536870920]],["^15",[1492,"^;","~u68123c08-2904-431b-9422-134aabee0492",536870920]],["^15",[1493,"^Q","It provides features like load balancing, service discovery, encryption, observability, and traffic management, allowing services to communicate securely and efficiently.",536870920]],["^15",[1493,"^O","^16",536870920]],["^15",[1493,"^F",1492,5368